 r←CBEditKeyPress args;id;event;key;txt;sel;msg;log
⍝ Dispatcher for DemoEditKeyPress.
⍝ The result is the KeyPress verdict: 0 vetoes the keystroke, anything else lets
⍝ it through (EWC/processEvent.aplf[109]). r is set on every path because the
⍝ function is declared with a result.

 r←1
 id←⊃args
 event←2⊃args

 :Select event
 :Case 'KeyPress'
     key←3⊃args
     ⍝ Text and SelText as seen from *inside* the callback: ⎕WC has not applied
     ⍝ the keystroke yet, so these describe the field before the key was pressed.
     (txt sel)←id eWG'Text' 'SelText'
     msg←'KeyPress ',(⍕key),' | WG Text="',(⍕txt),'" SelText=',⍕sel
     :If 'F1.DIGITS'≡id
     :AndIf 1=≢key           ⍝ never veto an input code - DB, LC, HT and friends
     :AndIf ~key∊⎕D
         r←0
         msg←'VETO ',msg
     :Else
         msg←'ok   ',msg
     :EndIf

 :Case 'Select'
     :Select id
     :Case 'F1.SETSEL'
         'F1.FREE'eWS'SelText'(3 5)
         msg←'WS F1.FREE SelText (3 5)'
     ⍝ Mode 2 - "perform default processing, do not invoke the callback" - which
     ⍝ is what "apply this key" means, and it also sets NoCallback so the client
     ⍝ does not echo the event back. Do not drop to Mode 0 here: the echo of a
     ⍝ single printable character arrives as Info ["Z"] and rank-errors in
     ⍝ EWC/processEvent.aplf[55], taking the interpreter down with it.
     :Case 'F1.NQCHAR'
         2 eNQ'F1.FREE' 'KeyPress' 'Z'
         msg←'NQ(2) F1.FREE KeyPress Z'
     :Case 'F1.NQBS'
         2 eNQ'F1.FREE' 'KeyPress' 'DB'
         msg←'NQ(2) F1.FREE KeyPress DB'
     :Case 'F1.SHOW'
         msg←'WG DIGITS Text="',(⍕'F1.DIGITS'eWG'Text'),'" FREE Text="',(⍕'F1.FREE'eWG'Text'),'" SelText=',⍕'F1.FREE'eWG'SelText'
     :EndSelect

 :Else
     msg←id,' ',event,': ',⍕2↓args
 :EndSelect

⍝ Prepend to the log label, keeping the last dozen lines (CBGrid.aplf:54-55).
 log←(⎕UCS 10)(≠⊆⊢)'F1.LOG'eWG'Caption'
 log←(⊂msg),(11⌊≢log)↑log
 'F1.LOG'eWS'Caption'(1↓∊(⎕UCS 10),¨log)
